      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after a local bachelor known as Ricks, who had recently died, giving Ricketts its unique name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ricketts_iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Within a year of its founding, Ricketts boasted a bank, a school, and even an opera house, reflecting its rapid growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ricketts_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ricketts sits along the Middle Soldier River, where flat prairie lands support the region’s agricultural productivity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
